<div>
<%= render 'organisations/shared/ai_area_header', title: t('views.organisations.ai_overview.pages.access') %>
<div class="flex justify-end items-center gap-2 mb-4">
  <%= render 'common/contextual_help_menu', context: :settings_ai_provider %>
  <%# No longer behind ai_enabled? — the probe is gate-free since S7 (L6), so the one
      moment it is most useful (setting up, before switching on) is no longer the one
      moment the button was hidden. The `provider:` query param went with it: it was
      never read, the action always resolved the org's own routing. %>
  <%= render Neo::Buttons::HeaderButtonComponent.new(
    variant: :primary,
    icon: "wifi",
    label: t('views.organisations.ai_settings.show.test_connection'),
    form: { action: test_connection_organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation), method: :post }
  ) %>
</div>

<%# The switch used to stand here as the largest box on the page (doc/ki_zugang_umbau_plan.md
    D5). It moved to the hub, and what stays behind is one line of orientation: this page
    answers "who processes our content, and where", and the switch is a decision about the
    whole area, not about the processor.

    The inactive line names the intended order explicitly (§3): the access can be set up
    BEFORE the switch is thrown, which is also why the connection test above is gate-free
    and why the hub's "Zugang" card stays unlocked while AI is off.

    No second truth here: the line states the boolean and links onwards, it repeats no
    date and no name (those live on the hub, with the switch). %>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-sm <%= @organisation.ai_enabled? ? 'text-cream-700' : 'text-amber-800' %>">
  <% unless @organisation.ai_enabled? %><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle mr-1.5"></i><% end %>
  <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.show.status_line_#{@organisation.ai_enabled? ? 'active' : 'inactive'}_html",
        link: link_to(t('views.organisations.ai_settings.show.status_line_overview_link'),
                      organisation_ai_overview_path(@organisation),
                      class: 'font-bold underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2')) %>
</p>

<%# Quota bar, evidence history and token statistics stood here until S6.
    They moved to "Verbrauch" (doc/ki_bereich_navigation_plan.md S6, L8); because
    of them the hub card "Verbrauch" pointed to the same page as "Zugang". %>

<%# KI-Pakete §7: the catalogue is the ONLY thing on this page that asks which processor
    serves the organisation. Until S7 it sat above a second form asking the same question
    with two axes; the setup screen that replaced that form is behind the custom pane.

    ONE pane per request (doc/ki_zugang_umbau_plan.md D6). The chooser above states the
    either/or, and exactly one of the two answers is rendered below it. Spelled out as a
    branch rather than interpolated into the partial name: @package_mode comes off a
    whitelist, and a render path built from a param is the kind of thing that only stays
    safe as long as the whitelist stays where somebody remembers it. %>
<div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl" id="ai_packages">
  <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/package_chooser' %>
  <% if @package_mode == Organisations::AiSettingsController::MODE_CUSTOM %>
    <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/package_pane_custom' %>
  <% else %>
    <%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/package_pane_packages' %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# The two-axis form and its inline <script> stood here until S7
    (doc/ki_bereich_navigation_plan.md, E6 Weg A). They moved to a setup screen of
    their own, not copied: the catalogue above asks the question "which package?",
    and the form asked it a second time below, with a provider select AND a
    system/own radio that a script switched against each other. Five of the
    thirteen gaps (L3, L5, L6, L7, L10) lived in it.
    The card "Eigene Konfiguration" in the catalogue is the door there. %>
</div>
